{"accuracy": "\"Accuracy\" in the context of semantic segmentation refers to a metric used to evaluate the performance of classification tasks. It is a crucial measure that indicates how well a model is able to correctly identify and classify elements within a dataset.|Here is another description: Accuracy, in the context of binary classification, is a metric that represents the proportion of correct predictions (both true positives and true negatives) among the total number of cases examined.|Here is another description: Accuracy is a measure used in statistical analysis and machine learning to evaluate the performance of a classification model. It represents the proportion of correct predictions (both true positives and true negatives) among the total number of cases examined."},
