{"a_new_metric": "A new metric refers to a recently developed method or standard used for assessing performance or quality in a specific domain.|Here is another description: A new metric refers to an innovative approach or method introduced to evaluate or measure something more effectively. In the context of semantic segmentation, it implies a novel way to assess the performance or quality of segmentation algorithms.|Here is another description: A new metric refers to a recently developed method or standard used to assess the performance of a system or process. In this context, it specifically pertains to a novel approach for evaluating the effectiveness of semantic segmentation techniques.|Here is another description: A new metric refers to an innovative approach or standard introduced to assess the performance of semantic segmentation, a task in computer vision where the goal is to classify each pixel in an image into a category."},
