{"semantic_segmentation__consists_of__associating_a_class_label_to_each_pixel_of_a_given_image": "The phrase \"consists of\" indicates that semantic segmentation is fundamentally composed of the process of assigning class labels to individual pixels. This process is essential for generating a comprehensive understanding of the image content at a granular level."},
{"associating_a_class_label_to_each_pixel_of_a_given_image": "Associating a class label to each pixel of a given image means that every pixel in the image is analyzed and categorized based on the object or class it represents. This results in a new image where each pixel is color-coded or labeled according to its identified class, providing a detailed semantic map of the original image."},
