{"the_problem_of_pixel_labeling": "The problem of pixel labeling, also known as semantic segmentation, involves associating a class label to each pixel of a given image. This results in an output image where each pixel is labeled according to the object or scene element it represents. This task is crucial for applications like mobile robotics and autonomous vehicles, where accurate scene interpretation is necessary for decision-making and navigation."},
