{"a_common_metric_to_evaluate_the_results_of_classification": "A common metric to evaluate the results of classification refers to a standard method or measure used to assess the accuracy and effectiveness of classification algorithms. These metrics help in determining how well a model can distinguish between different classes or categories in a dataset."},
{"jaccard_index_ji__is_also_known_as__intersection_over_union": "\"Is also known as\" indicates that the subject, the Jaccard index (JI), has an alternative name or synonymous term that is widely recognized and used interchangeably within the field."},
{"intersection_over_union": "Intersection-over-Union is an alternative name for the Jaccard index (JI). It specifically refers to the ratio of the intersection of two sets to the union of the same two sets, which is a fundamental concept in measuring overlap in various applications, including image segmentation and object detection."},
{"global_accuracy_metrics": "Global accuracy metrics refer to the overall measures used to evaluate the performance of a classification model, such as the total number of correct predictions divided by the total number of predictions.|Here is another description: Global accuracy metrics refer to the overall measures used to evaluate the performance of a classification model across all classes. These metrics are commonly employed to assess how well a model is performing in general."},
