{"metrics": "Metrics refer to the various quantitative measures used to evaluate the performance of a system or model, particularly in the context of classification tasks where class frequencies may be unbalanced."},
{"metrics__are_evaluated__per_class": "The phrase \"are evaluated\" indicates the process by which these metrics are assessed or calculated. In this context, it means that the metrics are computed in a specific manner to ensure fair and unbiased results."},
{"per_class": "\"Per-class\" refers to the method of evaluating metrics individually for each class in a classification task. This approach helps to mitigate the bias that can occur when class frequencies are unbalanced, ensuring that each class is given equal consideration in the evaluation process."},
{"result": "The result refers to the outcome or value obtained from evaluating specific metrics, which in this context are assessed on a per-class basis to ensure fairness and accuracy in scenarios with unbalanced class frequencies."},
