{"selected_images__are_scattered_through__different_sequences_with_different_conditions": "The predicate \"are scattered through\" indicates the distribution method of the selected images across the dataset. This scattering ensures that the images are spread out over various sequences and conditions, providing a diverse training set."},
{"different_sequences_with_different_conditions": "The different sequences with different conditions include various illumination and weather scenarios such as clone, fog, morning, overcast, rain, and sunset. These sequences help in training models under a wide range of environmental conditions."},
{"different_conditions": "The subject \"different conditions\" refers to the various illumination and weather conditions simulated in the Virtual Kitti dataset to generate training data for machine learning models. These conditions are designed to mimic real-world scenarios and enhance the robustness of the models."},
{"different_conditions__are__clone_fog_morning_overcast_rain_and_sunset": "The predicate \"are\" simply indicates the existence or inclusion of the listed conditions within the dataset. It serves as a linking verb to connect the subject with the object, specifying that the dataset includes these particular conditions."},
{"clone_fog_morning_overcast_rain_and_sunset": "The object \"clone, fog, morning, overcast, rain and sunset\" represents the specific weather and illumination conditions included in the Virtual Kitti dataset. These conditions are used to train machine learning models, ensuring they can handle a wide range of environmental variables encountered in real-world applications."},
{"each_model": "Each model refers to the individual instances of the neural network models that are being discussed in the context. These models are part of a series of experiments aimed at evaluating different methods of feeding geometric information into the SegNet architecture."},
{"each_model__is_trained__independently_from_scratch_from_the_same_training_data": "The predicate 'is trained' describes the process by which each model undergoes training. This involves the adjustment of the model's parameters based on the provided training data to optimize its performance for the task at hand, which in this case is semantic segmentation."},
{"independently_from_scratch_from_the_same_training_data": "The object 'independently from scratch from the same training data' specifies the conditions under which the models are trained. It indicates that each model is trained separately, without any pre-existing knowledge or parameters (from scratch), using the identical set of training data. This ensures that the models are not influenced by any prior training and allows for a fair comparison of their performance."},
