{"this_paper__addresses__the_problem_of_measuring_the_accuracy_of_semantic_segmentation_of_images": "The predicate \"addresses\" indicates that the paper tackles or deals with a specific issue or problem. In this context, it signifies that the paper is concerned with finding solutions or proposing methods to evaluate the accuracy of semantic segmentation."},
{"the_problem_of_measuring_the_accuracy_of_semantic_segmentation_of_images": "The problem of measuring the accuracy of semantic segmentation of images refers to the challenge of assessing how well an image segmentation algorithm performs in correctly identifying and delineating different objects or regions within an image. This is crucial for applications like autonomous driving, where precise object boundaries are necessary."},
{"measuring_the_accuracy_of_semantic_segmentation": "Measuring the accuracy of semantic segmentation refers to the process of evaluating how well a semantic segmentation algorithm performs in correctly identifying and categorizing each pixel in an image into its corresponding class. This is crucial for assessing the effectiveness of various segmentation techniques."},
{"measuring_the_accuracy_of_semantic_segmentation__is__an_essential_aspect_when_comparing_different_segmentation_approaches": "The phrase \"is\" serves as a linking verb that connects the subject, measuring the accuracy of semantic segmentation, to its significance as described in the object. It emphasizes the importance of this measurement in the broader context of comparing different segmentation approaches."},
{"an_essential_aspect_when_comparing_different_segmentation_approaches": "An essential aspect when comparing different segmentation approaches indicates that accurately measuring semantic segmentation is a critical factor in determining the effectiveness and reliability of various segmentation methods. This measurement helps in identifying which approach performs better in terms of correctly labeling pixels and maintaining the integrity of object boundaries."},
{"we__present__a_new_metric_to_compute_the_jaccard_index_considering_the_border_regions_of_the_different_classes": "The predicate indicates the action taken by the subject, which is the presentation of a new metric. This action is significant as it introduces a novel method for evaluating the accuracy of semantic segmentation, particularly focusing on the border regions of different classes."},
{"a_new_metric_to_compute_the_jaccard_index_considering_the_border_regions_of_the_different_classes": "The object is the new metric proposed by the authors to compute the Jaccard index. This metric is designed to consider the border regions of different classes, aiming to improve both global and contour accuracy in semantic segmentation, especially in scenarios with unbalanced class frequencies."},
{"the_new_metric__leverages__global_and_contour_accuracy": "The predicate \"leverages\" indicates that the new metric utilizes or takes advantage of certain features to enhance its performance. In this context, it specifically leverages global and contour accuracy to provide a more comprehensive evaluation of segmentation quality."},
{"the_new_metric__is_suitable_for__unbalanced_class_frequencies": "The phrase \"is suitable for\" indicates that the new metric is designed to effectively handle or accommodate a specific condition or scenario, in this case, unbalanced class frequencies in semantic segmentation tasks."},
{"unbalanced_class_frequencies": "Unbalanced class frequencies refer to a common issue in machine learning and data analysis where the distribution of classes is skewed, meaning some classes have significantly more instances than others. This can pose challenges for model training and evaluation, particularly in tasks like semantic segmentation where accurate classification of all classes is crucial."},
{"we__present_results_for__several_cnn_models_using_two_public_datasets": "The predicate \"present results for\" indicates that the authors are sharing the outcomes or findings of their research, specifically related to the performance of certain models on given datasets."},
{"several_cnn_models_using_two_public_datasets": "The object \"several CNN models using two public datasets\" describes the specific focus of the results presented by the authors, which involve multiple Convolutional Neural Network models evaluated on two commonly available datasets for semantic segmentation tasks."},
{"the_proposed_metric": "The proposed metric is a new method introduced in the paper to measure the accuracy of semantic segmentation of images. It is designed to compute the Jaccard index by considering the border regions of different classes, making it suitable for scenarios with unbalanced class frequencies."},
{"the_proposed_metric__encodes_jointly__the_rate_of_correctly_labelled_pixels_and_how_homeomorphic_is_the_segmentation_to_the_real_object_boundaries": "The phrase \"encodes jointly\" describes how the proposed metric integrates two critical aspects of segmentation accuracy into a single measure. It combines both the rate of correctly labeled pixels and the homeomorphism of the segmentation to real object boundaries."},
{"the_rate_of_correctly_labelled_pixels_and_how_homeomorphic_is_the_segmentation_to_the_real_object_boundaries": "The rate of correctly labeled pixels refers to the proportion of pixels in the image that are accurately classified by the segmentation algorithm. Homeomorphism in this context means how closely the segmented boundaries match the true boundaries of objects in the image, ensuring that the segmentation is topologically consistent with the real objects."},
{"this_aspect": "The aspect refers to the new metric proposed in the paper for computing the Jaccard index, which considers border regions of different classes to enhance both global and contour accuracy. This metric is particularly designed to handle unbalanced class frequencies in semantic segmentation tasks."},
{"this_aspect__is_highly_relevant_to__segment_correctly_the_limits_of_the_road_its_lanes_or_the_sidewalk_for_autonomous_driving_applications": "The relevance here signifies the importance and applicability of the proposed metric in achieving accurate segmentation results. It highlights how critical this metric is for ensuring that segmentation aligns well with real object boundaries, which is essential for practical applications."},
{"segment_correctly_the_limits_of_the_road_its_lanes_or_the_sidewalk_for_autonomous_driving_applications": "Segmenting correctly the limits of the road, its lanes, or the sidewalk is crucial for autonomous driving applications. Accurate segmentation ensures that autonomous vehicles can navigate safely by distinguishing between different elements of the road infrastructure, thus enhancing the reliability and safety of autonomous driving systems."},
{"our_results": "Our results refer to the outcomes and findings presented in the paper regarding the new metric for computing the Jaccard index in semantic segmentation, particularly its effectiveness in measuring accuracy for different CNN models on public datasets."},
{"our_results__can_also_be_applied_to__other_contexts_beyond_urban_driving_like_indoor_navigation": "The phrase \"can also be applied to\" indicates that the results and metric discussed in the paper have broader applicability beyond their primary context. This suggests versatility and potential for use in various scenarios."},
